<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · British Isles</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of the Regni</h1><p class="st-meta">43 CE – 80 CE (approx.) · capital Noviomagus Reginorum (Chichester)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Client kingdom of Togidubnus in Sussex and Hampshire, a loyal ally of Rome after the conquest whose seat may have been the palace at Fishbourne.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the Roman invasion of 43, much of the former realm of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/atrebates-britain">Atrebates (Britain)</a> was entrusted to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/togidubnus">Togidubnus</a>, a British noble loyal to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tacitus">Tacitus</a> says that certain states were given to him and that he remained faithful down to his own day, and the region became a base for Roman operations along the south coast.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>An inscription from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chichester">Chichester</a> dedicating a temple to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/neptune">Neptune</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/minerva">Minerva</a> names <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/togidubnus">Tiberius Claudius Togidubnus</a> as great king in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a>, showing that he held Roman citizenship and royal status. His capital, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/noviomagus-reginorum">Noviomagus Reginorum</a>, grew into a Roman-style town, and the lavish villa at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fishbourne-roman-palace">Fishbourne</a>, with mosaics and formal gardens, has often been linked to him. The kingdom provided <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> with a stable and Romanised territory.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>When <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/togidubnus">Togidubnus</a> died, probably around 80, the client kingdom was absorbed into the province of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/roman-britain">Roman Britain</a>. Its lands were divided into civitates, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/regni">Regni</a> around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chichester">Chichester</a> and probably the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/belgae-britain">Belgae (Britain)</a> around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/winchester">Winchester</a>. Chichester remains the main town of the region.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 43 CE – 80 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">British Isles</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:60.56%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>43 CE – 80 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Noviomagus Reginorum (Chichester)</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Togidubnus</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Romano-Celtic polytheism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Common Brittonic, Latin</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>United Kingdom</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Regnenses, Kingdom of Togidubnus, Regini</dd></dl></aside></div>
